      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "OHOKA COBRA NZ (2) was far from disgraced when he came from the back row to be beaten less than 5m here last start. Draws much better and the last two times he started near the pegs he recorded a Newcastle win and a city placing. Should get every chance to show his best. RED SAPPHIRE (5) is going well having recorded minor placings the last four times he has raced outside of the city, missing narrowly at this circuit and distance last week. Primary contender. ALTA SIERRA (8) was held up and not far away last time. May be relying on luck from another second line draw but his circuit and distance statistics are encouraging. HEIDSIECK NZ (1) is up in grade but has come from this barrier to place in his last two outings at Newcastle and won over this distance the only time he raced here.",
